ot  going to remember it doesn't matter  I will maybe study something else and  some of those words will show up or I'll  go back to the old lesson again and  slowly these things will start to stick  so I think we do a great disservice to  language learners when we expect them to  remember what was taught or when  language learners expect of themselves  that they're gonna remember what they're  trying to learn  you won't you're just exposing yourself  to something and you'll go back and  revisit it again and forget it and go  back again and eventually these things  start to stick and so I think if we have  this attitude of exploring without  trying to retain anything actually in  the long run we will try to retain a lot  so maybe we should try to learn  languages backwards and that's all I  have to say and now we're going to  continue our walk now  [Music]
 

